// Therapist's Office: Returning to the Present

- "It seems like you both have very different perspectives, but there's love here, even in the tension." #speaker:Therapist #pigeon:PeggyP1 #rat:RockyP1
- "Rocky, you're carrying pressure from your family, your community, and trying to balance that with Peggy." #speaker:Therapist
- "Peggy, you're feeling neglected. Not just by Rocky's absence, but by the gap between your worlds." #speaker:Therapist
- "That doesn't make your struggles less real. You've had to adjust to a world that doesn't always feel safe." #speaker:Therapist

- "Yeah… where I live, I have to be careful all the time. Dodging people, watching for strays, making sure I'm not caught somewhere I can't fly out of." #speaker:Peggy #pigeon:PeggyP3
- "It's exhausting. Always looking over my shoulder." #speaker:Peggy

- "So when you say I was never there… you don't just mean company." #speaker:Rocky #pigeon:PeggyP1 #rat:RockyP7
- "You wanted me there because you felt scared." #speaker:Rocky

- "I didn't always feel safe. And I don't think I wanted to admit that." #speaker:Peggy #pigeon:PeggyP3

- "I thought providing meant food, a place to rest. I thought that was enough." #speaker:Rocky #pigeon:PeggyP1 #rat:RockyP3
- "But I wasn't there. Not really." #speaker:Rocky #rat:RockyP1
- "I don't want you to feel like you're alone in it." #speaker:Rocky #pigeon:PeggyP4 #rat:RockyP6

- "See what happens when you hear each other? That's the power of slowing down." #speaker:Therapist
- "For now, we'll focus on three areas." #speaker:Therapist
- "Emotional Safety. Appreciation. Shared Meaning." #speaker:Therapist
- "Imagine you go to sleep tonight and a miracle happens. Everything therapy would fix is fixed." #speaker:Therapist #pigeon:PeggyP4 #rat:RockyP4
- "When you wake up tomorrow, what's different?" #speaker:Therapist

- "It's quiet. Inside." #speaker:Peggy #pigeon:PeggyP3
- "She's not bracing. And I'm not proving." #speaker:Rocky #rat:RockyP6

